## Agent Memory

Learnings from past sessions live in `docs/agent-memory.md`, not here. This rule stays short on purpose – it loads into every session, and the memory file does not.

- **Before changing the build, tests, deploy, or scripts**, read the Gotchas section of `docs/agent-memory.md`.
- **Before a task that touches an area you haven't worked in**, skim the matching section there (project structure, command relationships, workflow preferences, writing style, DRY decisions, what worked).
- **At the end of every task session**, append new learnings to `docs/agent-memory.md` under the relevant heading. Don't ask – just do it. If nothing was learned, skip silently. Keep entries concise; remove entries that turn out to be wrong.

Do not add learnings to this file.
